<title>RUSSIA: Russia Jan-April oil output edges up to 97.1 mln T.</title>
<headline>Russia Jan-April oil output edges up to 97.1 mln T.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-05-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russian oil output in the first four months of 1997 was 0.2 percent higher than year-ago levels at 97.1 million tonnes (5.83 million barrels per day), the State Statistics Committee said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Russia refined 57.7 million tonnes (3.46 million bpd) of oil in January-April, down three percent from year-ago levels, it said.</p>
<p>The committee gave the following data --  </p>
<p>RUSSIA JAN-APRIL 1997 OIL PRODUCTION (MILLION TONNES)</p>
<p>								  as pct of</p>
<p>					Jan April 1997    Jan-April 1996</p>
<p> Oil					97.1		  100.2</p>
<p> Refined oil			    57.7		   97.0</p>
<p>  gasoline				 8.6		   97.0</p>
<p>  diesel				  15.2		   98.0</p>
<p>  heavy fuel oil			21.9		   96.0</p>
<p>  lubricants			     0.6		   81.0</p>
<p>Natural gas</p>
<p>  (billion cubic metres)	   203.0		   97.0</p>
<p> Gas condensate			  2.9		   99.7</p>
<p>--Moscow Newsroom +7095 941 8520</p>
</text>
